{"title":"2023 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/6/ef6fa8111285bd14cbfd1f904a20c615aaa87da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 13,AC = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74d66f5fcd25f505cd4f9f4941a66164e1d33bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, a rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is inscribed such that the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is maximized. The minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c2fda68910564ae2b54151769b7c43c7b4e685b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{WX}{XY}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"39\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b8278fb534dff8a40361446a9c2094065f6f4013.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(320);  pair A = (0,0); pair B = (13,0); pair C = (5,12); pair D = (5,6); pair E = (5,0); pair W = (2.5,6); pair X = (9,6); pair Y = (9,0); pair Z = (2.5,0);  draw(A--B--C--cycle, black+linewidth(1)); draw(W--X--Y--Z--cycle, blue+linewidth(1.2)); draw(C--D--E, dotted+linewidth(1));  draw(rightanglemark(C,D,W)); draw(rightanglemark(C,E,A));  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, S); label(&quot;$W$&quot;, W, NW); label(&quot;$X$&quot;, X, NE); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;, Y, S); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;, Z, S); [/asy]\" width=\"535\" height=\"498\" /> </center><p> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> must have two vertices on a side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and the other two vertices on each of the other two sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Assume WLOG that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbf526d2c5592fe6cf1f23bef4c68fcb47cf9465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z,Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. For simplicity, denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d0295292581a1d637080145dc754b46a7a1364e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = AB = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e4dfd72ebad1ebe9136726548dc0ebffdff781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\frac{168}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-height of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3cc6016109bf3efc8bfd7cebf0a6e8db895b006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX=ZY=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b0bbfdd86657f8fe972a004468bfbdc1e0813c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=WZ=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/434b43c3ed50dfcfe55a5a68619bfe75826a1aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. From similar triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e4ab68b233423c4746cf636d0a9eb99ddf40c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CWX}\\sim\\triangle{CAB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac114d802fceea52931e83bab05d4bbf4b0cef7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{CD}{CE} = \\frac{WX}{AB}\\implies \\frac{h-y}{h} = \\frac{x}{c}\\implies\\frac{\\frac{168}{c}-y}{\\frac{168}{c}}=\\frac{x}{c}\\implies x=\\frac{168c-c^2y}{168}.\\]\" width=\"552\" height=\"47\" /> So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e425336b461b1d4396681783eababa228d178d78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[WXYZ] = xy = \\left(\\frac{168c-c^2y}{168}\\right)y = \\frac{168cy-c^2y^2}{168},\\]\" width=\"397\" height=\"43\" /> which is minimized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337d9f6699fed7c6712d5b58f1e3f61e319f58e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{168c}{-2c^2}=\\frac{84}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"139\" height=\"40\" />. Substituting, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/44264c4dba18b643ce9a0bf32222892de9d69530.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{168c-c^2\\cdot\\frac{84}{c}}{168}=\\frac{84c}{168} = \\frac{c}{2},\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"41\" /> meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54df2dc7f28b36587811d9cc51e83cb2b3cb9eb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{WX}{XY} = \\frac{x}{y}=\\frac{\\frac{c}{2}}{\\frac{84}{c}} = \\frac{c^2}{168}=\\frac{169}{168}\\implies 169+168 = \\boxed{337}.\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"45\" /> Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/4/074b6970b4bdb441e26568ef68c6162707d50a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WYXZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> had two vertices on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d259eafa9d27fef253ddd7f36d64ea12252071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC,BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, then we still have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410ea55fc0a01c465ed8b454cb3cf70e237ef9f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[WXYZ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> maximized to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b026876ecd72352d38b81b4f1bb2a999db597f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[ABC]}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"40\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b30a25a75cbffd042d455728b7becbf9e1116fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{WX}{XY}=\\frac{14^2}{168},\\frac{15^2}{168}&gt;\\frac{169}{168}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"192\" height=\"41\" />, respectively.\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024432\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 151/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8276/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31918:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024432 and revision id 274648. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}